          "abstractOriginal": "We propose a rational comparison between several well-known machine-learning interatomic potentials (linear atomic cluster expansion, the Behler-Parrinello high-dimensional neural network potential, and the graph neural network-based MACE potential) by testing their performance for fitting classical potentials such as the Lennard-Jones and Stillinger-Weber potential. With this we assess their advantages and limitations regarding several aspects: varying training dataset size, robustness to noise, carbon footprint, as well as the ability to reproduce the radial distribution function as an example observable. Overall the MACE models are shown to most accurately reproduce the potential energy surface, with little sign of overfitting, but at a significant computational cost, highlighting important questions regarding the choice of models in computational materials science.",
          "abstractZh": "我们通过测试几种著名的机器学习原子间势（线性原子团簇扩展、Behler-Parrinello 高维神经网络势和基于图神经网络的 MACE 势）对它们拟合经典势（如 Lennard-Jones 和 Stillinger-Weber 势）的性能进行理性比较。 由此，我们评估了它们在几个方面的优点和局限性：不同的训练数据集大小、对噪声的鲁棒性、碳足迹，以及重现径向分布函数作为可观察示例的能力。总体而言，MACE 模型能够最准确地再现势能面，几乎没有过度拟合的迹象，但计算成本很高，这凸显了计算材料科学中模型选择的重要问题。",
          "articleSummary": "We propose a rational comparison between several well-known machine-learning interatomic potentials (linear atomic cluster expansion, the Behler-Parrinello high-dimensional neural network potential, and the graph neural network-based MACE potential) by testing their performance for fitting classical potentials such as the Lennard-Jones and Stillinger-Weber potential. With this we assess their advantages and limitations regarding several aspects: varying training dataset size, robustness to noise, carbon footprint, as well as the ability to reproduce the radial distribution function as an example observable. Overall the MACE models are shown to most accurately reproduce the potential energy surface, with little sign of overfitting, but at a significant computational cost, highlighting important questions regarding the choice of models in computational materials science.",
          "articleSummaryZh": "我们通过测试几种著名的机器学习原子间势（线性原子团簇扩展、Behler-Parrinello 高维神经网络势和基于图神经网络的 MACE 势）对它们拟合经典势（如 Lennard-Jones 和 Stillinger-Weber 势）的性能进行理性比较。 由此，我们评估了它们在几个方面的优点和局限性：不同的训练数据集大小、对噪声的鲁棒性、碳足迹，以及重现径向分布函数作为可观察示例的能力。总体而言，MACE 模型能够最准确地再现势能面，几乎没有过度拟合的迹象，但计算成本很高，这凸显了计算材料科学中模型选择的重要问题。",
          "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 neural network potential、MACE potential 展开。 We propose a rational comparison between several well-known machine-learning interatomic potentials (linear atomic cluster expansion, the Behler-Parrinello high-dimensional neural network potential, and the graph neural network-based MACE potential) by testing their performance for fitting classical potentials such as the Lennard-Jones and Stillinger-Weber potential.",
          "discussionFocusZh": "我们通过测试几种著名的机器学习原子间势（线性原子团簇扩展、Behler-Parrinello 高维神经网络势和基于图神经网络的 MACE 势）对它们拟合经典势（如 Lennard-Jones 和 Stillinger-Weber 势）的性能进行理性比较。 由此，我们评估了它们在几个方面的优点和局限性：不同的训练数据集大小、对噪声的鲁棒性、碳足迹，以及重现径向分布函数作为可观察示例的能力。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注神经网络势、MACE 势函数相关的基准数据集、评价指标、误差来源，以及不同模型在精度、效率和可迁移性之间的取舍。"
