          "abstractOriginal": "Predicting speciation in concentrated electrolytes requires accurate ion interactions and adequate sampling of slowly interconverting coordination environments. We combine Zn K-edge extended X-ray absorption fine structure (EXAFS) measurements with long-timescale molecular dynamics (MD) using machine-learning interatomic potentials to study aqueous ZnCl2 from dilute conditions to 30 m. We train revPBE-based DeepMD models with D3 corrections included or excluded for Zn-containing pairs and compare them with DPMD-SCAN, classical MD (CMD), and MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN. EXAFS calculations are benchmarked against hydrated and chloride-coordinated Zn reference complexes, then applied to MD ensembles alongside Zn-Cl coordination free-energy analysis. Increasing concentration reduces octahedral coordination, replaces water with chloride, and promotes chloride-bridged association. All three DeepMD models yield similar EXAFS at 3 m, but DPMD-SCAN shows greater transferability across concentrations, reproducing measured spectral trends, key features of mixed ZnCl2/LiCl spectra, and octahedral fractions consistent with other studies. DFT treatment strongly affects coordination free energies and aggregation; excluding Zn-related D3 corrections does not systematically improve EXAFS agreement. CMD shows larger spectral discrepancies and less consistent coordination trends. MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN improves upon CMD and yields spectra comparable to DPMD-SCAN, which provides more consistent agreement and greater computational efficiency. Neighbor-resolved analysis shows that distance disorder and scattering-path interference can produce similar EXAFS signatures for distinct coordination ensembles, highlighting the need for rigorous sampling and ensemble-averaged spectra to distinguish isolated from chloride-bridged Zn species.",
          "abstractZh": "预测浓电解质中的形态需要准确的离子相互作用和对缓慢相互转换的配位环境进行充分采样。我们使用机器学习原子间势将 Zn K 边扩展 X 射线吸收精细结构 (EXAFS) 测量与长时标分子动力学 (MD) 相结合，研究从稀释条件到 30 m 的 ZnCl2 水溶液。我们训练基于 revPBE 的 DeepMD 模型，其中包含或排除含 Zn 对的 D3 校正，并将它们与 DPMD-SCAN、经典 MD (CMD) 和 MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN 进行比较。 EXAFS 计算以水合和氯化物配位 Zn 参考络合物为基准，然后应用于 MD 系综以及 Zn-Cl 配位自由能分析。增加浓度会减少八面体配位，用氯化物代替水，并促进氯化物桥联。所有三个 DeepMD 模型在 3 m 处均产生类似的 EXAFS，但 DPMD-SCAN 显示出更大的跨浓度可转移性，再现了测量的光谱趋势、混合 ZnCl2/LiCl 光谱的关键特征以及与其他研究一致的八面体分数。 DFT 处理强烈影响配位自由能和聚集；排除与 Zn 相关的 D3 修正并不能系统地改善 EXAFS 一致性。 CMD 显示出较大的光谱差异和不太一致的协调趋势。 MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN 在 CMD 的基础上进行了改进，产生的光谱可与 DPMD-SCAN 相媲美，从而提供更一致的一致性和更高的计算效率。 邻域解析分析表明，距离无序和散射路径干扰可以为不同的配位系综产生类似的 EXAFS 特征，这突出表明需要严格采样和系综平均光谱来区分分离的和氯桥 Zn 物种。",
          "articleSummary": "Predicting speciation in concentrated electrolytes requires accurate ion interactions and adequate sampling of slowly interconverting coordination environments. We combine Zn K-edge extended X-ray absorption fine structure (EXAFS) measurements with long-timescale molecular dynamics (MD) using machine-learning interatomic potentials to study aqueous ZnCl2 from dilute conditions to 30 m. We train revPBE-based DeepMD models with D3 corrections included or excluded for Zn-containing pairs and compare them with DPMD-SCAN, classical MD (CMD), and MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN. EXAFS calculations are benchmarked against hydrated and chloride-coordinated Zn reference complexes, then applied to MD ensembles alongside Zn-Cl coordination free-energy analysis. Increasing concentration reduces octahedral coordination, replaces water with chloride, and promotes chloride-bridged association. All three DeepMD models yield similar EXAFS at 3 m, but DPMD-SCAN shows greater transferability across concentrations, reproducing measured spectral trends, key features of mixed ZnCl2/LiCl spectra, and octahedral fractions consistent with other studies. DFT treatment strongly affects coordination free energies and aggregation; excluding Zn-related D3 corrections does not systematically improve EXAFS agreement. CMD shows larger spectral discrepancies and less consistent coordination trends. MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN improves upon CMD and yields spectra comparable to DPMD-SCAN, which provides more consistent agreement and greater computational efficiency. Neighbor-resolved analysis shows that distance disorder and scattering-path interference can produce similar EXAFS signatures for distinct coordination ensembles, highlighting the need for rigorous sampling and ensemble-averaged spectra to distinguish isolated from chloride-bridged Zn species.",
          "articleSummaryZh": "预测浓电解质中的形态需要准确的离子相互作用和对缓慢相互转换的配位环境进行充分采样。我们使用机器学习原子间势将 Zn K 边扩展 X 射线吸收精细结构 (EXAFS) 测量与长时标分子动力学 (MD) 相结合，研究从稀释条件到 30 m 的 ZnCl2 水溶液。我们训练基于 revPBE 的 DeepMD 模型，其中包含或排除含 Zn 对的 D3 校正，并将它们与 DPMD-SCAN、经典 MD (CMD) 和 MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN 进行比较。 EXAFS 计算以水合和氯化物配位 Zn 参考络合物为基准，然后应用于 MD 系综以及 Zn-Cl 配位自由能分析。增加浓度会减少八面体配位，用氯化物代替水，并促进氯化物桥联。所有三个 DeepMD 模型在 3 m 处均产生类似的 EXAFS，但 DPMD-SCAN 显示出更大的跨浓度可转移性，再现了测量的光谱趋势、混合 ZnCl2/LiCl 光谱的关键特征以及与其他研究一致的八面体分数。 DFT 处理强烈影响配位自由能和聚集；排除与 Zn 相关的 D3 修正并不能系统地改善 EXAFS 一致性。 CMD 显示出较大的光谱差异和不太一致的协调趋势。 MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN 在 CMD 的基础上进行了改进，产生的光谱可与 DPMD-SCAN 相媲美，从而提供更一致的一致性和更高的计算效率。 邻域解析分析表明，距离无序和散射路径干扰可以为不同的配位系综产生类似的 EXAFS 特征，这突出表明需要严格采样和系综平均光谱来区分分离的和氯桥 Zn 物种。",
          "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 DeepMD 展开。 We combine Zn K-edge extended X-ray absorption fine structure (EXAFS) measurements with long-timescale molecular dynamics (MD) using machine-learning interatomic potentials to study aqueous ZnCl2 from dilute conditions to 30 m.",
          "discussionFocusZh": "我们使用机器学习原子间势将 Zn K 边扩展 X 射线吸收精细结构 (EXAFS) 测量与长时标分子动力学 (MD) 相结合，研究从稀释条件到 30 m 的 ZnCl2 水溶液。我们训练基于 revPBE 的 DeepMD 模型，其中包含或排除含 Zn 对的 D3 校正，并将它们与 DPMD-SCAN、经典 MD (CMD) 和 MACE-MATPES-r2SCAN 进行比较。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注DeepMD相关的基准数据集、评价指标、误差来源，以及不同模型在精度、效率和可迁移性之间的取舍。"
