          "abstractOriginal": "The two-dimensional Hubbard model was originally proposed as the minimal model of uniform $d$-wave superconductivity in the cuprate high-temperature superconductors, but recent calculations with relevant parameters in a realistic doping regime have often found other ground states. Further, uncertainty remains over such results due to the intrinsic bias of different computational methods. Here we address this uncertainty through state-of-the-art neural tensor network and neural backflow state simulations, enabled by large-scale GPU computation, that together reach an unprecedented variational accuracy on lattices with up to 1024 sites. At $1/8$ doping in the pure Hubbard model, as well as with next-nearest-neighbor hopping relevant to the hole-doped cuprates, we reveal a near degeneracy among a low-energy uniform $d$-wave state, superconducting stripes, and non-superconducting stripe states on the milli-$t$ energy scale. Our work rebalances the narrative that the Hubbard model supports a single dominant order in relevant parameter regimes towards a picture of extreme competition between stripes and superconductivity.",
          "abstractZh": "二维哈伯德模型最初被提出作为铜酸盐高温超导体中均匀 $d$ 波超导性的最小模型，但最近在实际掺杂体系中使用相关参数进行的计算经常发现其他基态。此外，由于不同计算方法的固有偏差，这些结果仍然存在不确定性。 在这里，我们通过大规模 GPU 计算实现的最先进的神经张量网络和神经回流状态模拟来解决这种不确定性，这些模拟在多达 1024 个位点的晶格上共同达到了前所未有的变分精度。在纯哈伯德模型中的 $1/8$ 掺杂以及与空穴掺杂铜酸盐相关的次近邻跳跃时，我们揭示了毫 $t$ 能量尺度上低能均匀 $d$ 波态、超导条带和非超导条带态之间的近简并性。 我们的工作重新平衡了哈伯德模型在相关参数体系中支持单一主导顺序的叙述，以描绘条纹和超导性之间的极端竞争图景。",
          "articleSummary": "The two-dimensional Hubbard model was originally proposed as the minimal model of uniform $d$-wave superconductivity in the cuprate high-temperature superconductors, but recent calculations with relevant parameters in a realistic doping regime have often found other ground states. Further, uncertainty remains over such results due to the intrinsic bias of different computational methods. Here we address this uncertainty through state-of-the-art neural tensor network and neural backflow state simulations, enabled by large-scale GPU computation, that together reach an unprecedented variational accuracy on lattices with up to 1024 sites. At $1/8$ doping in the pure Hubbard model, as well as with next-nearest-neighbor hopping relevant to the hole-doped cuprates, we reveal a near degeneracy among a low-energy uniform $d$-wave state, superconducting stripes, and non-superconducting stripe states on the milli-$t$ energy scale. Our work rebalances the narrative that the Hubbard model supports a single dominant order in relevant parameter regimes towards a picture of extreme competition between stripes and superconductivity.",
