              "abstractOriginal": "Diamond is an important host material for functional defects such as solid-state spin qubits. During the defect creation by irradiation and subsequent thermal annealing, carbon-related defects, including vacancies and interstitials, are generated and can migrate to form new defect complexes. To investigate this kinetically driven process and reveal the formation mechanisms of the di-interstitials and di-vacancies in the neutral charge state, we fine-tuned a universal machine learning interatomic potential using a small dataset generated from density functional theory calculations. We obtained a barrier of 1.84 eV for mono-interstitial migration and found that two initially separated mono-interstitials only need to overcome a lower barrier to form di-interstitial configurations. Beyond the training data, the MLIP also identified the formation pathway for an additional di-interstitial configuration and a stepwise divacancy dissociation mechanism. These results reveal migration-assisted defect complex formation mechanisms and demonstrate how targeted MLIP training can identify reaction pathways.",
              "abstractZh": "金刚石是固态自旋量子位等功能缺陷的重要主体材料。在通过辐射和随后的热退火产生缺陷的过程中，会产生与碳相关的缺陷，包括空位和填隙，并且可以迁移形成新的缺陷复合体。为了研究这种动力学驱动的过程并揭示中性电荷态双填隙和双空位的形成机制，我们使用密度泛函理论计算生成的小数据集对通用机器学习原子间势进行了微调。 我们获得了单填隙迁移的势垒为 1.84 eV，并发现两个最初分离的单填隙只需克服较低的势垒即可形成双填隙构型。除了训练数据之外，MLIP 还确定了额外的双间隙构型和逐步双空位解离机制的形成途径。这些结果揭示了迁移辅助缺陷复合体形成机制，并证明了有针对性的 MLIP 训练如何识别反应途径。",
              "articleSummary": "Diamond is an important host material for functional defects such as solid-state spin qubits. During the defect creation by irradiation and subsequent thermal annealing, carbon-related defects, including vacancies and interstitials, are generated and can migrate to form new defect complexes. To investigate this kinetically driven process and reveal the formation mechanisms of the di-interstitials and di-vacancies in the neutral charge state, we fine-tuned a universal machine learning interatomic potential using a small dataset generated from density functional theory calculations. We obtained a barrier of 1.84 eV for mono-interstitial migration and found that two initially separated mono-interstitials only need to overcome a lower barrier to form di-interstitial configurations. Beyond the training data, the MLIP also identified the formation pathway for an additional di-interstitial configuration and a stepwise divacancy dissociation mechanism. These results reveal migration-assisted defect complex formation mechanisms and demonstrate how targeted MLIP training can identify reaction pathways.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "金刚石是固态自旋量子位等功能缺陷的重要主体材料。在通过辐射和随后的热退火产生缺陷的过程中，会产生与碳相关的缺陷，包括空位和填隙，并且可以迁移形成新的缺陷复合体。为了研究这种动力学驱动的过程并揭示中性电荷态双填隙和双空位的形成机制，我们使用密度泛函理论计算生成的小数据集对通用机器学习原子间势进行了微调。 我们获得了单填隙迁移的势垒为 1.84 eV，并发现两个最初分离的单填隙只需克服较低的势垒即可形成双填隙构型。除了训练数据之外，MLIP 还确定了额外的双间隙构型和逐步双空位解离机制的形成途径。这些结果揭示了迁移辅助缺陷复合体形成机制，并证明了有针对性的 MLIP 训练如何识别反应途径。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 machine learning interatomic potential 展开。 To investigate this kinetically driven process and reveal the formation mechanisms of the di-interstitials and di-vacancies in the neutral charge state, we fine-tuned a universal machine learning interatomic potential using a small dataset generated from density functional theory calculations.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "为了研究这种动力学驱动的过程并揭示中性电荷态双填隙和双空位的形成机制，我们使用密度泛函理论计算生成的小数据集对通用机器学习原子间势进行了微调。在通过辐射和随后的热退火产生缺陷的过程中，会产生与碳相关的缺陷，包括空位和填隙，并且可以迁移形成新的缺陷复合体。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注机器学习原子间势相关的第一性原理设置、对称性分析、能带或响应函数计算，以及这些量与可观测物性的对应关系。"
