              "abstractOriginal": "The continued demand for smaller, faster, and more energy-efficient technologies has driven condensed-matter research towards materials combining multiple responses within a single phase. Particularly interesting examples are multiferroic materials featuring cross-couplings between order parameters. Ni3TeO6 is a prominent member of this material class, exhibiting a hysteresis-free transition under magnetic field which simultaneously affects the magnetic structure, electric polarization, and phonon frequencies. Here, we uncover the microscopic origin of this multiferroic transition using a combination of neutron scattering techniques. We establish the presence of a finite Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya exchange term giving rise to non-reciprocal, chiral spin waves which soften in magnetic field. Their condensation alters the magnetic structure which controls the electric polarization and drives an ionic displacement, thereby coupling the magnetic, electric, and lattice degrees of freedom. Our study demonstrates that neutron scattering is a powerful technique to elucidate microscopic interactions in multiferroic materials, informing the design of next-generation electronic devices.",
              "abstractZh": "对更小、更快、更节能技术的持续需求推动了凝聚态物质研究转向在单相内结合多种响应的材料。特别有趣的例子是具有有序参数之间交叉耦合的多铁材料。 Ni3TeO6 是此类材料的重要成员，在磁场下表现出无磁滞转变，同时影响磁结构、电极化和声子频率。 在这里，我们结合中子散射技术揭示了这种多铁性转变的微观起源。我们确定了有限 Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya 交换项的存在，该交换项产生了在磁场中软化的非互易手性自旋波。它们的凝结改变了控制电极化并驱动离子位移的磁性结构，从而耦合了磁、电和晶格自由度。 我们的研究表明，中子散射是一种强大的技术，可以阐明多铁材料中的微观相互作用，为下一代电子设备的设计提供信息。",
              "articleSummary": "The continued demand for smaller, faster, and more energy-efficient technologies has driven condensed-matter research towards materials combining multiple responses within a single phase. Particularly interesting examples are multiferroic materials featuring cross-couplings between order parameters. Ni3TeO6 is a prominent member of this material class, exhibiting a hysteresis-free transition under magnetic field which simultaneously affects the magnetic structure, electric polarization, and phonon frequencies. Here, we uncover the microscopic origin of this multiferroic transition using a combination of neutron scattering techniques. We establish the presence of a finite Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya exchange term giving rise to non-reciprocal, chiral spin waves which soften in magnetic field. Their condensation alters the magnetic structure which controls the electric polarization and drives an ionic displacement, thereby coupling the magnetic, electric, and lattice degrees of freedom. Our study demonstrates that neutron scattering is a powerful technique to elucidate microscopic interactions in multiferroic materials, informing the design of next-generation electronic devices.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "对更小、更快、更节能技术的持续需求推动了凝聚态物质研究转向在单相内结合多种响应的材料。特别有趣的例子是具有有序参数之间交叉耦合的多铁材料。 Ni3TeO6 是此类材料的重要成员，在磁场下表现出无磁滞转变，同时影响磁结构、电极化和声子频率。 在这里，我们结合中子散射技术揭示了这种多铁性转变的微观起源。我们确定了有限 Dzyaloshinskii-Moriya 交换项的存在，该交换项产生了在磁场中软化的非互易手性自旋波。它们的凝结改变了控制电极化并驱动离子位移的磁性结构，从而耦合了磁、电和晶格自由度。 我们的研究表明，中子散射是一种强大的技术，可以阐明多铁材料中的微观相互作用，为下一代电子设备的设计提供信息。",
