              "abstractOriginal": "Binary tree states have been introduced as compact correlated pair wave functions that improve upon the antisymmetrized geminal power by adding variational flexibility. Here, we extend the binary tree state to the fermionic half-filled Hubbard model using restricted and unrestricted orbitals. Although the ansatz is seniority zero in its optimized pairing basis, its expansion in the original Hubbard site basis can contain nonzero site- seniority character, while unrestricted orbital optimization provides additional flexibility through independent spin-up and spin-down orbitals. This provides a mechanism for a paired ansatz to describe the singly occupied configurations that dominate the repulsive Hubbard model at large U/t. We find that unrestricted BTS closely approaches optimized DOCI in the repulsive regime, substantially improves upon AGP, and reproduces DOCI density correlations more accurately than pCCD",
              "abstractZh": "二叉树状态已被引入作为紧凑相关对波函数，通过增加变分灵活性来改进反对称孪生功率。在这里，我们使用受限和非受限轨道将二叉树状态扩展到费米子半填充哈伯德模型。尽管 ansatz 在其优化配对基础上的资历为零，但其在原始哈伯德站点基础上的扩展可以包含非零站点资历特征，而不受限制的轨道优化通过独立的自旋向上和自旋向下轨道提供了额外的灵活性。 这为配对 ansatz 提供了一种机制来描述在大 U/t 下主导排斥哈伯德模型的单占据配置。我们发现，不受限制的 BTS 在排斥状态下非常接近优化的 DOCI，大大改进了 AGP，并且比 pCCD 更准确地再现了 DOCI 密度相关性",
              "articleSummary": "Binary tree states have been introduced as compact correlated pair wave functions that improve upon the antisymmetrized geminal power by adding variational flexibility. Here, we extend the binary tree state to the fermionic half-filled Hubbard model using restricted and unrestricted orbitals. Although the ansatz is seniority zero in its optimized pairing basis, its expansion in the original Hubbard site basis can contain nonzero site- seniority character, while unrestricted orbital optimization provides additional flexibility through independent spin-up and spin-down orbitals. This provides a mechanism for a paired ansatz to describe the singly occupied configurations that dominate the repulsive Hubbard model at large U/t. We find that unrestricted BTS closely approaches optimized DOCI in the repulsive regime, substantially improves upon AGP, and reproduces DOCI density correlations more accurately than pCCD",
