          "abstractOriginal": "Accurate atomistic simulations of materials under electric fields require long-range electrostatics and electrical-response modeling at length scales beyond the reach of conventional first-principles methods. Yet these capabilities remain difficult to reconcile with the scalability of machine-learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs). Strictly local models enable efficient spatial parallelization but neglect long-range interactions, whereas existing electrostatic extensions introduce global dependencies that hinder distributed computation. Here, we overcome this limitation by analytically separating the long-range electrostatic forces and Born effective charges (BECs) into a global electrostatics calculation and strictly local derivatives of learned latent charges. This formulation preserves the spatial decomposability of equivariant MLIPs while enabling distributed evaluation of energies, forces, stresses, and BECs across different boundary conditions. Implemented as DPA4C-LR on the \\texttt{nvalchemi} platform, the framework scales to 5.2 million atoms on four GPUs at approximately twice the computational cost of its short-range backbone. Trained on energies and forces, DPA4C-LR accurately infers BECs and reproduces the field-dependent infrared spectra of water. We further demonstrate its capabilities by recovering the characteristic slim polarization hysteresis of relaxor \\ce{Pb(Mg_{1/3}Nb_{2/3})O3}, which is obscured by finite-size effects in smaller simulations; predicting a room-temperature field-driven ionic conductivity of $6.8 \\pm 0.7$~mS/cm in amorphous \\ce{Li_{0.9}NbO_{0.9}Cl_{4.1}}; and modeling interfacial thermal transport across Si/diamond interfaces with slab-corrected electrostatics. By combining long-range physics, electrical-response inference, and distributed computation, this framework extends predictive atomistic modeling toward device-relevant length scales.",
          "abstractZh": "在电场下对材料进行精确的原子模拟需要在长度尺度上进行长程静电和电响应建模，这超出了传统第一原理方法的范围。然而，这些功能仍然难以与机器学习原子间势（MLIP）的可扩展性相协调。严格的局部模型可以实现高效的空间并行化，但忽略了远程交互，而现有的静电扩展引入了阻碍分布式计算的全局依赖性。 在这里，我们通过分析将长程静电力和玻恩有效电荷（BEC）分离为全局静电计算和学习潜电荷的严格局部导数来克服这一限制。该公式保留了等变 MLIP 的空间可分解性，同时能够跨不同边界条件对能量、力、应力和 BEC 进行分布式评估。 该框架在 \\texttt{nvalchemi} 平台上以 DPA4C-LR 的形式实现，可在四个 GPU 上扩展到 520 万个原子，其计算成本约为其短程主干的两倍。经过能量和力的训练，DPA4C-LR 可以准确推断 BEC 并再现水的场相关红外光谱。 我们通过恢复弛豫器 \\ce{Pb(Mg_{1/3}Nb_{2/3})O3} 特有的微小极化滞后来进一步证明其功能，该滞后在较小的模拟中被有限尺寸效应所掩盖；预测非晶态 \\ce{Li_{0.9}NbO_{0.9}Cl_{4.1}} 中室温场驱动离子电导率为 $6.8 \\pm 0.7$~mS/cm；并利用平板校正静电对跨硅/金刚石界面的界面热传输进行建模。",
          "articleSummary": "Accurate atomistic simulations of materials under electric fields require long-range electrostatics and electrical-response modeling at length scales beyond the reach of conventional first-principles methods. Yet these capabilities remain difficult to reconcile with the scalability of machine-learning interatomic potentials (MLIPs). Strictly local models enable efficient spatial parallelization but neglect long-range interactions, whereas existing electrostatic extensions introduce global dependencies that hinder distributed computation. Here, we overcome this limitation by analytically separating the long-range electrostatic forces and Born effective charges (BECs) into a global electrostatics calculation and strictly local derivatives of learned latent charges. This formulation preserves the spatial decomposability of equivariant MLIPs while enabling distributed evaluation of energies, forces, stresses, and BECs across different boundary conditions. Implemented as DPA4C-LR on the \\texttt{nvalchemi} platform, the framework scales to 5.2 million atoms on four GPUs at approximately twice the computational cost of its short-range backbone. Trained on energies and forces, DPA4C-LR accurately infers BECs and reproduces the field-dependent infrared spectra of water. We further demonstrate its capabilities by recovering the characteristic slim polarization hysteresis of relaxor \\ce{Pb(Mg_{1/3}Nb_{2/3})O3}, which is obscured by finite-size effects in smaller simulations; predicting a room-temperature field-driven ionic conductivity of $6.8 \\pm 0.7$~mS/cm in amorphous \\ce{Li_{0.9}NbO_{0.9}Cl_{4.1}}; and modeling interfacial thermal transport across Si/diamond interfaces with slab-corrected electrostatics. By combining long-range physics, electrical-response inference, and distributed computation, this framework extends predictive atomistic modeling toward device-relevant length scales.",
          "articleSummaryZh": "在电场下对材料进行精确的原子模拟需要在长度尺度上进行长程静电和电响应建模，这超出了传统第一原理方法的范围。然而，这些功能仍然难以与机器学习原子间势（MLIP）的可扩展性相协调。严格的局部模型可以实现高效的空间并行化，但忽略了远程交互，而现有的静电扩展引入了阻碍分布式计算的全局依赖性。 在这里，我们通过分析将长程静电力和玻恩有效电荷（BEC）分离为全局静电计算和学习潜电荷的严格局部导数来克服这一限制。该公式保留了等变 MLIP 的空间可分解性，同时能够跨不同边界条件对能量、力、应力和 BEC 进行分布式评估。 该框架在 \\texttt{nvalchemi} 平台上以 DPA4C-LR 的形式实现，可在四个 GPU 上扩展到 520 万个原子，其计算成本约为其短程主干的两倍。经过能量和力的训练，DPA4C-LR 可以准确推断 BEC 并再现水的场相关红外光谱。 我们通过恢复弛豫器 \\ce{Pb(Mg_{1/3}Nb_{2/3})O3} 特有的微小极化滞后来进一步证明其功能，该滞后在较小的模拟中被有限尺寸效应所掩盖；预测非晶态 \\ce{Li_{0.9}NbO_{0.9}Cl_{4.1}} 中室温场驱动离子电导率为 $6.8 \\pm 0.7$~mS/cm；并利用平板校正静电对跨硅/金刚石界面的界面热传输进行建模。",
          "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 machine learning interatomic potential 展开。 Strictly local models enable efficient spatial parallelization but neglect long-range interactions, whereas existing electrostatic extensions introduce global dependencies that hinder distributed computation.",
          "discussionFocusZh": "严格的局部模型可以实现高效的空间并行化，但忽略了远程交互，而现有的静电扩展引入了阻碍分布式计算的全局依赖性。该框架在 \\texttt{nvalchemi} 平台上以 DPA4C-LR 的形式实现，可在四个 GPU 上扩展到 520 万个原子，其计算成本约为其短程主干的两倍。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注机器学习原子间势相关的第一性原理设置、对称性分析、能带或响应函数计算，以及这些量与可观测物性的对应关系。"
