              "abstractOriginal": "Oxygen-vacancy formation and diffusion play important roles in determining the electronic and atomic transport properties of SrTiO$_3$ (STO). Accurate analysis of such point defects requires sufficiently large-scale and long-time molecular dynamics (MD) simulations; however, direct investigations of oxygen-vacancy dynamics using {\\it ab initio} MD (AIMD) based on density functional theory (DFT) are limited to relatively small systems and short time scales because of their high computational cost. In this study, we develop a neural network potential (NNP) for pristine and oxygen-deficient STO using a reference dataset generated from AIMD simulations. The trained NNP model accurately reproduces the DFT reference energies, atomic forces, and virials for both pristine STO and STO containing an oxygen vacancy. The NNP also reproduces the supercell-size dependence of the total energies and oxygen-vacancy formation energies, including the formation energy extrapolated to the dilute limit. Large-scale and long-time MD simulations using the NNP (NNP-MD) are then performed to investigate oxygen-vacancy diffusion. The resulting oxygen-vacancy diffusion coefficients show substantially better agreement with experimental data than those obtained from conventional classical MD simulations. An Arrhenius analysis yields an oxygen-vacancy migration enthalpy of 0.64 eV, in close agreement with the experimental value of 0.67 eV. These results demonstrate that NNPs trained on first-principles data provide an accurate and computationally efficient framework for investigating defect formation and long-time vacancy transport in perovskite oxides.",
              "abstractZh": "氧空位的形成和扩散在确定 SrTiO$_3$ (STO) 的电子和原子输运特性方面发挥着重要作用。对此类点缺陷的精确分析需要足够大规模和长时间的分子动力学（MD）模拟；然而，基于密度泛函理论（DFT）的从头开始MD（AIMD）对氧空位动力学的直接研究仅限于相对较小的系统和较短的时间尺度，因为其计算成本较高。 在这项研究中，我们使用 AIMD 模拟生成的参考数据集开发了用于原始缺氧 STO 的神经网络潜力 (NNP)。经过训练的 NNP 模型准确地再现了原始 STO 和包含氧空位的 STO 的 DFT 参考能量、原子力和维里尔。 NNP 还再现了总能量和氧空位形成能的超晶胞尺寸依赖性，包括外推到稀极限的形成能。 然后使用 NNP (NNP-MD) 进行大规模和长时间的 MD 模拟，以研究氧空位扩散。与传统经典 MD 模拟获得的氧空位扩散系数相比，所得氧空位扩散系数与实验数据的吻合程度要好得多。阿伦尼乌斯分析得出氧空位迁移焓为 0.64 eV，与实验值 0.67 eV 非常一致。 这些结果表明，基于第一原理数据训练的 NNP 为研究钙钛矿氧化物中的缺陷形成和长期空位传输提供了准确且计算高效的框架。",
              "articleSummary": "Oxygen-vacancy formation and diffusion play important roles in determining the electronic and atomic transport properties of SrTiO$_3$ (STO). Accurate analysis of such point defects requires sufficiently large-scale and long-time molecular dynamics (MD) simulations; however, direct investigations of oxygen-vacancy dynamics using {\\it ab initio} MD (AIMD) based on density functional theory (DFT) are limited to relatively small systems and short time scales because of their high computational cost. In this study, we develop a neural network potential (NNP) for pristine and oxygen-deficient STO using a reference dataset generated from AIMD simulations. The trained NNP model accurately reproduces the DFT reference energies, atomic forces, and virials for both pristine STO and STO containing an oxygen vacancy. The NNP also reproduces the supercell-size dependence of the total energies and oxygen-vacancy formation energies, including the formation energy extrapolated to the dilute limit. Large-scale and long-time MD simulations using the NNP (NNP-MD) are then performed to investigate oxygen-vacancy diffusion. The resulting oxygen-vacancy diffusion coefficients show substantially better agreement with experimental data than those obtained from conventional classical MD simulations. An Arrhenius analysis yields an oxygen-vacancy migration enthalpy of 0.64 eV, in close agreement with the experimental value of 0.67 eV. These results demonstrate that NNPs trained on first-principles data provide an accurate and computationally efficient framework for investigating defect formation and long-time vacancy transport in perovskite oxides.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "氧空位的形成和扩散在确定 SrTiO$_3$ (STO) 的电子和原子输运特性方面发挥着重要作用。对此类点缺陷的精确分析需要足够大规模和长时间的分子动力学（MD）模拟；然而，基于密度泛函理论（DFT）的从头开始MD（AIMD）对氧空位动力学的直接研究仅限于相对较小的系统和较短的时间尺度，因为其计算成本较高。 在这项研究中，我们使用 AIMD 模拟生成的参考数据集开发了用于原始缺氧 STO 的神经网络潜力 (NNP)。经过训练的 NNP 模型准确地再现了原始 STO 和包含氧空位的 STO 的 DFT 参考能量、原子力和维里尔。 NNP 还再现了总能量和氧空位形成能的超晶胞尺寸依赖性，包括外推到稀极限的形成能。 然后使用 NNP (NNP-MD) 进行大规模和长时间的 MD 模拟，以研究氧空位扩散。与传统经典 MD 模拟获得的氧空位扩散系数相比，所得氧空位扩散系数与实验数据的吻合程度要好得多。阿伦尼乌斯分析得出氧空位迁移焓为 0.64 eV，与实验值 0.67 eV 非常一致。 这些结果表明，基于第一原理数据训练的 NNP 为研究钙钛矿氧化物中的缺陷形成和长期空位传输提供了准确且计算高效的框架。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 neural network potential 展开。 In this study, we develop a neural network potential (NNP) for pristine and oxygen-deficient STO using a reference dataset generated from AIMD simulations.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "在这项研究中，我们使用 AIMD 模拟生成的参考数据集开发了用于原始缺氧 STO 的神经网络潜力 (NNP)。经过训练的 NNP 模型准确地再现了原始 STO 和包含氧空位的 STO 的 DFT 参考能量、原子力和维里尔。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注神经网络势相关的模拟体系、时间尺度、温度条件、动力学稳定性，以及有限温度性质对势函数质量的敏感性。"
