              "abstractOriginal": "The sign problem poses a fundamental barrier to numerically exact quantum Monte Carlo simulations, severely hindering our understanding of quantum many-body physics across disciplines ranging from condensed matter to particle and nuclear physics. Geometrical frustration makes this barrier especially acute for interacting bosons. Here, we develop a bosonic auxiliary-field quantum Monte Carlo (BAFQMC) method and rigorously prove that time-reversal symmetry and reflection positivity each provide a general sufficient condition for sign-problem-free simulations. Crucially, under either criterion, BAFQMC evades the sign problem even on frustrated lattices where conventional world-line and stochastic-series-expansion methods fail. Benchmarking our approach on a two-flavor Bose-Hubbard model on the triangular lattice yields excellent quantitative agreement with finite-temperature exact diagonalization. By establishing unifying principles to solve the sign problem in BAFQMC, our work substantially expands the reach of unbiased, numerically exact simulations for frustrated bosonic matter.",
              "abstractZh": "符号问题对数值精确的量子蒙特卡罗模拟构成了根本障碍，严重阻碍了我们对从凝聚态物理到粒子物理和核物理等跨学科的量子多体物理的理解。几何挫败使得这种障碍对于相互作用的玻色子来说尤其严重。在这里，我们开发了一种玻色子辅助场量子蒙特卡罗（BAFQMC）方法，并严格证明时间反转对称性和反射正性都为无符号问题模拟提供了一般充分条件。 至关重要的是，在任一标准下，即使在传统世界线和随机级数展开方法失败的受挫格上，BAFQMC 也能避免符号问题。对三角晶格上的两种 Bose-Hubbard 模型的方法进行基准测试，得到了与有限温度精确对角化的良好定量一致性。通过建立统一原则来解决 BAFQMC 中的符号问题，我们的工作大大扩展了受挫玻色物质的无偏、数值精确模拟的范围。",
              "articleSummary": "The sign problem poses a fundamental barrier to numerically exact quantum Monte Carlo simulations, severely hindering our understanding of quantum many-body physics across disciplines ranging from condensed matter to particle and nuclear physics. Geometrical frustration makes this barrier especially acute for interacting bosons. Here, we develop a bosonic auxiliary-field quantum Monte Carlo (BAFQMC) method and rigorously prove that time-reversal symmetry and reflection positivity each provide a general sufficient condition for sign-problem-free simulations. Crucially, under either criterion, BAFQMC evades the sign problem even on frustrated lattices where conventional world-line and stochastic-series-expansion methods fail. Benchmarking our approach on a two-flavor Bose-Hubbard model on the triangular lattice yields excellent quantitative agreement with finite-temperature exact diagonalization. By establishing unifying principles to solve the sign problem in BAFQMC, our work substantially expands the reach of unbiased, numerically exact simulations for frustrated bosonic matter.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "符号问题对数值精确的量子蒙特卡罗模拟构成了根本障碍，严重阻碍了我们对从凝聚态物理到粒子物理和核物理等跨学科的量子多体物理的理解。几何挫败使得这种障碍对于相互作用的玻色子来说尤其严重。在这里，我们开发了一种玻色子辅助场量子蒙特卡罗（BAFQMC）方法，并严格证明时间反转对称性和反射正性都为无符号问题模拟提供了一般充分条件。 至关重要的是，在任一标准下，即使在传统世界线和随机级数展开方法失败的受挫格上，BAFQMC 也能避免符号问题。对三角晶格上的两种 Bose-Hubbard 模型的方法进行基准测试，得到了与有限温度精确对角化的良好定量一致性。通过建立统一原则来解决 BAFQMC 中的符号问题，我们的工作大大扩展了受挫玻色物质的无偏、数值精确模拟的范围。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 Hubbard model、quantum many-body 展开。 Here, we develop a bosonic auxiliary-field quantum Monte Carlo (BAFQMC) method and rigorously prove that time-reversal symmetry and reflection positivity each provide a general sufficient condition for sign-problem-free simulations.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "在这里，我们开发了一种玻色子辅助场量子蒙特卡罗（BAFQMC）方法，并严格证明时间反转对称性和反射正性都为无符号问题模拟提供了一般充分条件。几何挫败使得这种障碍对于相互作用的玻色子来说尤其严重。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注Hubbard 模型、量子多体相关的有效模型参数、电子关联强度、相图边界以及可与实验对照的谱学或输运信号。"
