          "abstractOriginal": "Permutationally invariant polynomials (PIPs) provide a systematically improvable, symmetry-preserving representation for global potential energy surfaces (PESs), but their high computational cost as neural network descriptors limits applications to large molecular systems. Fundamental invariants (FIs), which form an algebraically complete generating set, substantially reduce the number of descriptors and enable neural network PESs for larger systems. However, PES evaluation remains computationally expensive as molecular size and complexity increase. Here, we introduce recursive separating invariants (RSIs), shifting the descriptor design principle from algebraic completeness to orbit separation. RSIs are constructed systematically through correlation order and recursion depth, providing a more computationally efficient representation. Benchmarks on reactive and nonreactive systems demonstrate that RSI-based neural network (RSI-NN) PESs achieve approximately an order-of-magnitude faster evaluation than their FI-NN counterparts, with system-dependent prediction accuracy that is comparable in several cases. These results establish orbit separation as a promising principle for developing efficient symmetry-preserving descriptors for global neural network PESs.",
          "abstractZh": "置换不变多项式 (PIP) 为全局势能面 (PES) 提供了系统可改进的、保持对称性的表示，但其作为神经网络描述符的高计算成本限制了其在大型分子系统中的应用。基本不变量 (FI) 形成代数完备的生成集，大大减少了描述符的数量，并使神经网络 PES 能够用于更大的系统。然而，随着分子尺寸和复杂性的增加，PES 评估的计算成本仍然很高。 在这里，我们引入了递归分离不变量（RSI），将描述符设计原则从代数完备性转变为轨道分离。 RSI 是通过相关顺序和递归深度系统构建的，提供了计算效率更高的表示。反应性和非反应性系统的基准测试表明，基于 RSI 的神经网络 (RSI-NN) PES 的评估速度比 FI-NN 同类产品快大约一个数量级，并且系统相关的预测精度在多种情况下相当。 这些结果确立了轨道分离作为为全局神经网络 PES 开发有效的对称性保持描述符的有前途的原理。",
          "articleSummary": "Permutationally invariant polynomials (PIPs) provide a systematically improvable, symmetry-preserving representation for global potential energy surfaces (PESs), but their high computational cost as neural network descriptors limits applications to large molecular systems. Fundamental invariants (FIs), which form an algebraically complete generating set, substantially reduce the number of descriptors and enable neural network PESs for larger systems. However, PES evaluation remains computationally expensive as molecular size and complexity increase. Here, we introduce recursive separating invariants (RSIs), shifting the descriptor design principle from algebraic completeness to orbit separation. RSIs are constructed systematically through correlation order and recursion depth, providing a more computationally efficient representation. Benchmarks on reactive and nonreactive systems demonstrate that RSI-based neural network (RSI-NN) PESs achieve approximately an order-of-magnitude faster evaluation than their FI-NN counterparts, with system-dependent prediction accuracy that is comparable in several cases. These results establish orbit separation as a promising principle for developing efficient symmetry-preserving descriptors for global neural network PESs.",
          "articleSummaryZh": "置换不变多项式 (PIP) 为全局势能面 (PES) 提供了系统可改进的、保持对称性的表示，但其作为神经网络描述符的高计算成本限制了其在大型分子系统中的应用。基本不变量 (FI) 形成代数完备的生成集，大大减少了描述符的数量，并使神经网络 PES 能够用于更大的系统。然而，随着分子尺寸和复杂性的增加，PES 评估的计算成本仍然很高。 在这里，我们引入了递归分离不变量（RSI），将描述符设计原则从代数完备性转变为轨道分离。 RSI 是通过相关顺序和递归深度系统构建的，提供了计算效率更高的表示。反应性和非反应性系统的基准测试表明，基于 RSI 的神经网络 (RSI-NN) PES 的评估速度比 FI-NN 同类产品快大约一个数量级，并且系统相关的预测精度在多种情况下相当。 这些结果确立了轨道分离作为为全局神经网络 PES 开发有效的对称性保持描述符的有前途的原理。",
          "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 neural network potential 展开。 Here, we introduce recursive separating invariants (RSIs), shifting the descriptor design principle from algebraic completeness to orbit separation.",
          "discussionFocusZh": "在这里，我们引入了递归分离不变量（RSI），将描述符设计原则从代数完备性转变为轨道分离。基本不变量 (FI) 形成代数完备的生成集，大大减少了描述符的数量，并使神经网络 PES 能够用于更大的系统。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注神经网络势相关的基准数据集、评价指标、误差来源，以及不同模型在精度、效率和可迁移性之间的取舍。"
