          "abstractOriginal": "Developing a machine learning interatomic potential (MLIP) that is accurate for the specific conditions under which it will be applied, rather than simply for the predefined configurations chosen by the model developer, is a significant challenge in atomistic simulation. Active learning (AL) addresses this challenge by closing the loop between candidate generation, data selection, reference calculation, and model updating. Here, we survey more than seventy studies, with an emphasis on work from 2020 to 2026, to understand how active learning has evolved from a niche, on-the-fly training technique for query-by-committee and Gaussian process force fields into a diverse family of data-efficient strategies. he reviewed examples include on-the-fly molecular dynamics, active data selection for fine-tuning pretrained models, kernel- and representation-based acquisition using frozen pretrained models, and reaction-aware sampling for chemical systems far from equilibrium. We explore the use of active learning in elemental and alloy mechanics, hydrogen and ion diffusion, ferroelectrics and effective Hamiltonians of functional materials, reactive and photochemical dynamics, high-entropy and compositionally disordered materials, as well as generative and autonomous material discovery pipelines. Drawing on a growing body of critical, methodologically self-aware literature, we also show that this achievement carries systematic caveats. Uncertainty estimates are not interchangeable across model architectures and are frequently the least reliable exactly where they matter most. We close by discussing the outlook for standardized, uncertainty-calibrated, and observable-targeted active-learning workflows in the foundation-model era.",
          "abstractZh": "开发一种机器学习原子间势 (MLIP)，使其能够准确地适应其应用的特定条件，而不仅仅是模型开发人员选择的预定义配置，这是原子模拟中的一项重大挑战。主动学习 (AL) 通过关闭候选生成、数据选择、参考计算和模型更新之间的循环来解决这一挑战。 在这里，我们调查了 70 多项研究，重点关注 2020 年至 2026 年的工作，以了解主动学习如何从针对委员会查询和高斯过程力场的利基动态训练技术演变为多种数据高效策略。他回顾的例子包括动态分子动力学、用于微调预训练模型的主动数据选择、使用冻结预训练模型进行基于内核和表示的采集，以及远离平衡的化学系统的反应感知采样。 我们探索主动学习在元素和合金力学、氢和离子扩散、铁电体和功能材料的有效哈密顿量、反应和光化学动力学、高熵和成分无序材料以及生成和自主材料发现管道中的应用。借鉴越来越多的批判性、方法论上自我意识的文献，我们还表明，这一成就带有系统性的警告。 不确定性估计在模型架构之间不可互换，并且在最重要的地方往往是最不可靠的。最后，我们讨论了基础模型时代标准化、不确定性校准和可观察目标的主动学习工作流程的前景。",
          "articleSummary": "Developing a machine learning interatomic potential (MLIP) that is accurate for the specific conditions under which it will be applied, rather than simply for the predefined configurations chosen by the model developer, is a significant challenge in atomistic simulation. Active learning (AL) addresses this challenge by closing the loop between candidate generation, data selection, reference calculation, and model updating. Here, we survey more than seventy studies, with an emphasis on work from 2020 to 2026, to understand how active learning has evolved from a niche, on-the-fly training technique for query-by-committee and Gaussian process force fields into a diverse family of data-efficient strategies. he reviewed examples include on-the-fly molecular dynamics, active data selection for fine-tuning pretrained models, kernel- and representation-based acquisition using frozen pretrained models, and reaction-aware sampling for chemical systems far from equilibrium. We explore the use of active learning in elemental and alloy mechanics, hydrogen and ion diffusion, ferroelectrics and effective Hamiltonians of functional materials, reactive and photochemical dynamics, high-entropy and compositionally disordered materials, as well as generative and autonomous material discovery pipelines. Drawing on a growing body of critical, methodologically self-aware literature, we also show that this achievement carries systematic caveats. Uncertainty estimates are not interchangeable across model architectures and are frequently the least reliable exactly where they matter most. We close by discussing the outlook for standardized, uncertainty-calibrated, and observable-targeted active-learning workflows in the foundation-model era.",
          "articleSummaryZh": "开发一种机器学习原子间势 (MLIP)，使其能够准确地适应其应用的特定条件，而不仅仅是模型开发人员选择的预定义配置，这是原子模拟中的一项重大挑战。主动学习 (AL) 通过关闭候选生成、数据选择、参考计算和模型更新之间的循环来解决这一挑战。 在这里，我们调查了 70 多项研究，重点关注 2020 年至 2026 年的工作，以了解主动学习如何从针对委员会查询和高斯过程力场的利基动态训练技术演变为多种数据高效策略。他回顾的例子包括动态分子动力学、用于微调预训练模型的主动数据选择、使用冻结预训练模型进行基于内核和表示的采集，以及远离平衡的化学系统的反应感知采样。 我们探索主动学习在元素和合金力学、氢和离子扩散、铁电体和功能材料的有效哈密顿量、反应和光化学动力学、高熵和成分无序材料以及生成和自主材料发现管道中的应用。借鉴越来越多的批判性、方法论上自我意识的文献，我们还表明，这一成就带有系统性的警告。 不确定性估计在模型架构之间不可互换，并且在最重要的地方往往是最不可靠的。最后，我们讨论了基础模型时代标准化、不确定性校准和可观察目标的主动学习工作流程的前景。",
          "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 machine learning interatomic potential 展开。 We explore the use of active learning in elemental and alloy mechanics, hydrogen and ion diffusion, ferroelectrics and effective Hamiltonians of functional materials, reactive and photochemical dynamics, high-entropy and compositionally disordered materials, as well as generative and autonomous material discovery pipelines.",
          "discussionFocusZh": "我们探索主动学习在元素和合金力学、氢和离子扩散、铁电体和功能材料的有效哈密顿量、反应和光化学动力学、高熵和成分无序材料以及生成和自主材料发现管道中的应用。开发一种机器学习原子间势 (MLIP)，使其能够准确地适应其应用的特定条件，而不仅仅是模型开发人员选择的预定义配置，这是原子模拟中的一项重大挑战。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注机器学习原子间势相关的极化翻转、磁电耦合、自旋-晶格耦合以及多铁序参量之间的相互制约。"
