              "abstractOriginal": "Defect engineering is a crucial tool for tuning and tailoring the properties of two-dimensional (2D) materials. A key challenge is identifying which defects are kinetically stable at room temperature and sufficiently promising to warrant further investigation. However, identifying stable defects with suitable properties using first-principles calculations, such as density functional theory (DFT) is computationally demanding, effectively limiting the scope of high-throughput studies. In this work, we investigate whether the machine learning interatomic potential MACE can reproduce sorption trends (adsorption vs. absorption) previously obtained from high-throughput DFT calculations and extend the analysis to elevated temperatures. A total of 17,624 defect structures from the ADAQ database are simulated using MACE-accelerated molecular dynamics (MD) at both 0 K and 300 K. The results show that MACE successfully reproduces the overall sorption trends observed in DFT calculations at 0 K at a fraction of the computational cost. Simulations performed at 300 K further indicate that the qualitative sorption trends remain largely the same when including finite-temperature effects. These findings demonstrate that MACE-driven MD can be used as an effective high-throughput prescreening tool for defect-related studies in 2D materials, specially related to sorption. While conventional first-principles methods, such as DFT, remain necessary for accurate and quantitative validation, the use of MLIPs enables MD simulations of finite-temperature defect behavior at a fraction of the computational cost of DFT-based MD.",
              "abstractZh": "缺陷工程是调整和定制二维 (2D) 材料性能的重要工具。一个关键的挑战是确定哪些缺陷在室温下是动力学稳定的，并且有足够的前景值得进一步研究。然而，使用第一原理计算（例如密度泛函理论（DFT））来识别具有合适特性的稳定缺陷的计算要求很高，有效地限制了高通量研究的范围。 在这项工作中，我们研究了机器学习原子间势 MACE 是否可以重现先前从高通量 DFT 计算中获得的吸附趋势（吸附与吸收），并将分析扩展到高温。使用 MACE 加速分子动力学 (MD) 在 0 K 和 300 K 下模拟了 ADAQ 数据库中总共 17,624 个缺陷结构。结果表明，MACE 成功地重现了 0 K 下 DFT 计算中观察到的总体吸附趋势，而计算成本仅为一小部分。 在 300 K 下进行的模拟进一步表明，当考虑有限温度效应时，定性吸附趋势基本保持不变。这些发现表明，MACE 驱动的 MD 可用作二维材料缺陷相关研究的有效高通量预筛选工具，特别是与吸附相关的研究。虽然传统的第一原理方法（例如 DFT）仍然是准确和定量验证所必需的，但使用 MLIP 可以对有限温度缺陷行为进行 MD 模拟，而计算成本仅为基于 DFT 的 MD 的一小部分。",
              "articleSummary": "Defect engineering is a crucial tool for tuning and tailoring the properties of two-dimensional (2D) materials. A key challenge is identifying which defects are kinetically stable at room temperature and sufficiently promising to warrant further investigation. However, identifying stable defects with suitable properties using first-principles calculations, such as density functional theory (DFT) is computationally demanding, effectively limiting the scope of high-throughput studies. In this work, we investigate whether the machine learning interatomic potential MACE can reproduce sorption trends (adsorption vs. absorption) previously obtained from high-throughput DFT calculations and extend the analysis to elevated temperatures. A total of 17,624 defect structures from the ADAQ database are simulated using MACE-accelerated molecular dynamics (MD) at both 0 K and 300 K. The results show that MACE successfully reproduces the overall sorption trends observed in DFT calculations at 0 K at a fraction of the computational cost. Simulations performed at 300 K further indicate that the qualitative sorption trends remain largely the same when including finite-temperature effects. These findings demonstrate that MACE-driven MD can be used as an effective high-throughput prescreening tool for defect-related studies in 2D materials, specially related to sorption. While conventional first-principles methods, such as DFT, remain necessary for accurate and quantitative validation, the use of MLIPs enables MD simulations of finite-temperature defect behavior at a fraction of the computational cost of DFT-based MD.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "缺陷工程是调整和定制二维 (2D) 材料性能的重要工具。一个关键的挑战是确定哪些缺陷在室温下是动力学稳定的，并且有足够的前景值得进一步研究。然而，使用第一原理计算（例如密度泛函理论（DFT））来识别具有合适特性的稳定缺陷的计算要求很高，有效地限制了高通量研究的范围。 在这项工作中，我们研究了机器学习原子间势 MACE 是否可以重现先前从高通量 DFT 计算中获得的吸附趋势（吸附与吸收），并将分析扩展到高温。使用 MACE 加速分子动力学 (MD) 在 0 K 和 300 K 下模拟了 ADAQ 数据库中总共 17,624 个缺陷结构。结果表明，MACE 成功地重现了 0 K 下 DFT 计算中观察到的总体吸附趋势，而计算成本仅为一小部分。 在 300 K 下进行的模拟进一步表明，当考虑有限温度效应时，定性吸附趋势基本保持不变。这些发现表明，MACE 驱动的 MD 可用作二维材料缺陷相关研究的有效高通量预筛选工具，特别是与吸附相关的研究。虽然传统的第一原理方法（例如 DFT）仍然是准确和定量验证所必需的，但使用 MLIP 可以对有限温度缺陷行为进行 MD 模拟，而计算成本仅为基于 DFT 的 MD 的一小部分。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 machine learning interatomic potential 展开。 In this work, we investigate whether the machine learning interatomic potential MACE can reproduce sorption trends (adsorption vs. absorption) previously obtained from high-throughput DFT calculations and extend the analysis to elevated temperatures.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "在这项工作中，我们研究了机器学习原子间势 MACE 是否可以重现先前从高通量 DFT 计算中获得的吸附趋势（吸附与吸收），并将分析扩展到高温。一个关键的挑战是确定哪些缺陷在室温下是动力学稳定的，并且有足够的前景值得进一步研究。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注机器学习原子间势相关的模拟体系、时间尺度、温度条件、动力学稳定性，以及有限温度性质对势函数质量的敏感性。"
