              "abstractOriginal": "Away from half filling and above its Neel temperature, the three-dimensional Hubbard model is a paramagnetic metal with antiferromagnetic spin fluctuations, where controlled momentum-resolved results have been lacking. Using connected-determinant diagrammatic Monte Carlo, we compute the momentum-resolved self-energy for n = 0.4-0.95, T/t = 0.05-0.33 and U/t = 4-8, and the full-zone spin susceptibility at twelve of these points, focusing on U/t = 4. At U/t = 4 and toward half filling the spin fluctuations become strong: for n = 0.7-0.9 at T/t = 0.14 they enhance the susceptibility peak up to sevenfold and raise the momentum-dependent part of the scattering rate to four to five times its second-order value. They are driven by an effective spin interaction screened to about 2U/3 and nearly uniform over the zone. Yet the peak height is set by the slightly smaller value of this interaction at the peak wave vector, and near magnetic order this small difference changes the height by a large factor. Two-particle self-consistent theory reproduces the peak because its sum rule fixes its single constant interaction near this value, but for n = 0.7-0.9 at T/t = 0.14 its self-energy overestimates the local scattering rate and underestimates the momentum-dependent part. Though strong, the fluctuations are short ranged, with a correlation length of at most about two lattice spacings, and for n = 0.7-0.9 and T/t >= 0.14 the scattering rate near the Fermi surface varies by at most about 1% at fixed band energy, without hot spots. At U/t = 4 dynamical mean-field theory (DMFT) reproduces the local scattering rate and quasiparticle weight within a few percent, and the nonlocal part it misses is approximately a function of the band energy. Strong spin fluctuations thus coexist with nearly isotropic quasiparticles, and the results provide a benchmark for extensions of DMFT and for spin-fluctuation theories.",
              "abstractZh": "远离半填充且高于尼尔温度，三维哈伯德模型是一种具有反铁磁自旋涨落的顺磁性金属，其中缺乏受控动量解析结果。使用连通行列式蒙特卡罗图，我们计算了 n = 0.4-0.95、T/t = 0.05-0.33 和 U/t = 4-8 的动量分辨自能，以及其中 12 个点的全区自旋敏感性，重点关注 U/t = 4。 在 U/t = 4 和接近半填充时，自旋波动变得更强：对于 n = 0.7-0.9，在 T/t = 0.14 时，它们将磁化率峰值增强至七倍，并将散射率的动量相关部分提高至其二阶值的四到五倍。它们由有效的自旋相互作用驱动，该自旋相互作用筛选至约 2U/3 并且在整个区域上几乎均匀。然而，峰值高度是由峰值波矢量处的这种相互作用的稍小的值决定的，并且在磁阶附近，这种微小的差异会以很大的系数改变高度。 双粒子自洽理论再现了峰值，因为它的求和规则将其单一常数相互作用固定在该值附近，但对于 n = 0.7-0.9，T/t = 0.14，其自能高估了局部散射率并低估了动量相关部分。虽然波动很强，但波动范围很短，相关长度最多约为两个晶格间距，并且对于 n = 0.7-0.9 且 T/t >= 0.14，费米表面附近的散射率在固定带能量下最多变化约 1%，没有热点。 当 U/t = 4 时，动态平均场理论 (DMFT) 在百分之几内重现了局部散射率和准粒子重量，并且它错过的非局部部分大约是能带能量的函数。因此，强自旋涨落与近各向同性准粒子共存，其结果为 DMFT 的扩展和自旋涨落理论提供了基准。",
              "articleSummary": "Away from half filling and above its Neel temperature, the three-dimensional Hubbard model is a paramagnetic metal with antiferromagnetic spin fluctuations, where controlled momentum-resolved results have been lacking. Using connected-determinant diagrammatic Monte Carlo, we compute the momentum-resolved self-energy for n = 0.4-0.95, T/t = 0.05-0.33 and U/t = 4-8, and the full-zone spin susceptibility at twelve of these points, focusing on U/t = 4. At U/t = 4 and toward half filling the spin fluctuations become strong: for n = 0.7-0.9 at T/t = 0.14 they enhance the susceptibility peak up to sevenfold and raise the momentum-dependent part of the scattering rate to four to five times its second-order value. They are driven by an effective spin interaction screened to about 2U/3 and nearly uniform over the zone. Yet the peak height is set by the slightly smaller value of this interaction at the peak wave vector, and near magnetic order this small difference changes the height by a large factor. Two-particle self-consistent theory reproduces the peak because its sum rule fixes its single constant interaction near this value, but for n = 0.7-0.9 at T/t = 0.14 its self-energy overestimates the local scattering rate and underestimates the momentum-dependent part. Though strong, the fluctuations are short ranged, with a correlation length of at most about two lattice spacings, and for n = 0.7-0.9 and T/t >= 0.14 the scattering rate near the Fermi surface varies by at most about 1% at fixed band energy, without hot spots. At U/t = 4 dynamical mean-field theory (DMFT) reproduces the local scattering rate and quasiparticle weight within a few percent, and the nonlocal part it misses is approximately a function of the band energy. Strong spin fluctuations thus coexist with nearly isotropic quasiparticles, and the results provide a benchmark for extensions of DMFT and for spin-fluctuation theories.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "远离半填充且高于尼尔温度，三维哈伯德模型是一种具有反铁磁自旋涨落的顺磁性金属，其中缺乏受控动量解析结果。使用连通行列式蒙特卡罗图，我们计算了 n = 0.4-0.95、T/t = 0.05-0.33 和 U/t = 4-8 的动量分辨自能，以及其中 12 个点的全区自旋敏感性，重点关注 U/t = 4。 在 U/t = 4 和接近半填充时，自旋波动变得更强：对于 n = 0.7-0.9，在 T/t = 0.14 时，它们将磁化率峰值增强至七倍，并将散射率的动量相关部分提高至其二阶值的四到五倍。它们由有效的自旋相互作用驱动，该自旋相互作用筛选至约 2U/3 并且在整个区域上几乎均匀。然而，峰值高度是由峰值波矢量处的这种相互作用的稍小的值决定的，并且在磁阶附近，这种微小的差异会以很大的系数改变高度。 双粒子自洽理论再现了峰值，因为它的求和规则将其单一常数相互作用固定在该值附近，但对于 n = 0.7-0.9，T/t = 0.14，其自能高估了局部散射率并低估了动量相关部分。虽然波动很强，但波动范围很短，相关长度最多约为两个晶格间距，并且对于 n = 0.7-0.9 且 T/t >= 0.14，费米表面附近的散射率在固定带能量下最多变化约 1%，没有热点。 当 U/t = 4 时，动态平均场理论 (DMFT) 在百分之几内重现了局部散射率和准粒子重量，并且它错过的非局部部分大约是能带能量的函数。因此，强自旋涨落与近各向同性准粒子共存，其结果为 DMFT 的扩展和自旋涨落理论提供了基准。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 Hubbard model 展开。 Strong spin fluctuations thus coexist with nearly isotropic quasiparticles, and the results provide a benchmark for extensions of DMFT and for spin-fluctuation theories.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "因此，强自旋涨落与近各向同性准粒子共存，其结果为 DMFT 的扩展和自旋涨落理论提供了基准。远离半填充且高于尼尔温度，三维哈伯德模型是一种具有反铁磁自旋涨落的顺磁性金属，其中缺乏受控动量解析结果。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注Hubbard 模型相关的有效模型参数、电子关联强度、相图边界以及可与实验对照的谱学或输运信号。"
