              "abstractOriginal": "Continuous-time Quantum Monte Carlo (CTQMC) impurity solvers are a numerically exact, but expensive, option for solving the Dynamical Mean Field Theory (DMFT) equations, with statistical noise from undersampling presenting a major challenge to low temperature studies. This noise is especially egregious within the sampled self-energy, which can destabilize the self-consistency loop upon insertion into the Dyson equation. In this work, we introduce a neural denoiser for fermionic imaginary time Green's functions based on the diffusion model architecture trained on synthetic data. The network predicts positive and normalized auxiliary spectral functions consistent with the noisy imaginary axis CTQMC data, which is then refined via autodifferentiation to match the measured self-energy, its first two high-frequency moments, and impurity occupation similar to the Constrained Residual Minimization (CRM) method. This leads to Green's functions and self-energies that are causal by design. Through this denoising framework we are able to reduce the required CTQMC measurement steps by a factor of 10-100. We benchmark our method with a half-filled Hubbard model on a Bethe lattice, a two-patch Dynamical Cluster Approximation (DCA) of the two-dimensional Hubbard model, and the SrVO$_3$ system. We reproduce the Mott transition upon increasing Coulomb interaction for the half-filled Hubbard model with only 5000 CTQMC measurements, the pseudogap transition for the DCA two-dimensional Hubbard model with only 5$\\times$10$^5$ measurements, and match the spectral function of SrVO$_3$ with 50 times fewer measurements than the reference. Since we generate auxiliary spectral functions, we recover the approximate spectral functions of the systems for free without performing analytic continuation.",
              "abstractZh": "连续时间量子蒙特卡罗 (CTQMC) 杂质求解器是求解动态平均场理论 (DMFT) 方程的数值精确但昂贵的选择，欠采样产生的统计噪声给低温研究带来了重大挑战。这种噪声在采样的自能中尤其严重，在插入戴森方程时可能会破坏自洽环的稳定性。在这项工作中，我们基于在合成数据上训练的扩散模型架构，引入了费米子虚数时间格林函数的神经降噪器。 该网络预测与噪声虚轴 CTQMC 数据一致的正和归一化辅助谱函数，然后通过自微分进行细化，以匹配测量的自能、前两个高频矩以及类似于约束残差最小化 (CRM) 方法的杂质占据。这导致了格林函数和自能是设计上的因果关系。通过这个去噪框架，我们能够将所需的 CTQMC 测量步骤减少 10-100 倍。 我们使用 Bethe 晶格上的半填充 Hubbard 模型、二维 Hubbard 模型的两面片动态聚类近似 (DCA) 以及 SrVO$_3$ 系统对我们的方法进行基准测试。我们通过仅 5000 个 CTQMC 测量的半填充 Hubbard 模型在增加库仑相互作用时重现莫特跃迁，仅用 5$\\times$10$^5$ 测量的 DCA 二维 Hubbard 模型的赝能隙跃迁，并以比参考少 50 倍的测量来匹配 SrVO$_3$ 的谱函数。 由于我们生成辅助谱函数，因此我们可以免费恢复系统的近似谱函数，而无需执行解析延拓。",
              "articleSummary": "Continuous-time Quantum Monte Carlo (CTQMC) impurity solvers are a numerically exact, but expensive, option for solving the Dynamical Mean Field Theory (DMFT) equations, with statistical noise from undersampling presenting a major challenge to low temperature studies. This noise is especially egregious within the sampled self-energy, which can destabilize the self-consistency loop upon insertion into the Dyson equation. In this work, we introduce a neural denoiser for fermionic imaginary time Green's functions based on the diffusion model architecture trained on synthetic data. The network predicts positive and normalized auxiliary spectral functions consistent with the noisy imaginary axis CTQMC data, which is then refined via autodifferentiation to match the measured self-energy, its first two high-frequency moments, and impurity occupation similar to the Constrained Residual Minimization (CRM) method. This leads to Green's functions and self-energies that are causal by design. Through this denoising framework we are able to reduce the required CTQMC measurement steps by a factor of 10-100. We benchmark our method with a half-filled Hubbard model on a Bethe lattice, a two-patch Dynamical Cluster Approximation (DCA) of the two-dimensional Hubbard model, and the SrVO$_3$ system. We reproduce the Mott transition upon increasing Coulomb interaction for the half-filled Hubbard model with only 5000 CTQMC measurements, the pseudogap transition for the DCA two-dimensional Hubbard model with only 5$\\times$10$^5$ measurements, and match the spectral function of SrVO$_3$ with 50 times fewer measurements than the reference. Since we generate auxiliary spectral functions, we recover the approximate spectral functions of the systems for free without performing analytic continuation.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "连续时间量子蒙特卡罗 (CTQMC) 杂质求解器是求解动态平均场理论 (DMFT) 方程的数值精确但昂贵的选择，欠采样产生的统计噪声给低温研究带来了重大挑战。这种噪声在采样的自能中尤其严重，在插入戴森方程时可能会破坏自洽环的稳定性。在这项工作中，我们基于在合成数据上训练的扩散模型架构，引入了费米子虚数时间格林函数的神经降噪器。 该网络预测与噪声虚轴 CTQMC 数据一致的正和归一化辅助谱函数，然后通过自微分进行细化，以匹配测量的自能、前两个高频矩以及类似于约束残差最小化 (CRM) 方法的杂质占据。这导致了格林函数和自能是设计上的因果关系。通过这个去噪框架，我们能够将所需的 CTQMC 测量步骤减少 10-100 倍。 我们使用 Bethe 晶格上的半填充 Hubbard 模型、二维 Hubbard 模型的两面片动态聚类近似 (DCA) 以及 SrVO$_3$ 系统对我们的方法进行基准测试。我们通过仅 5000 个 CTQMC 测量的半填充 Hubbard 模型在增加库仑相互作用时重现莫特跃迁，仅用 5$\\times$10$^5$ 测量的 DCA 二维 Hubbard 模型的赝能隙跃迁，并以比参考少 50 倍的测量来匹配 SrVO$_3$ 的谱函数。 由于我们生成辅助谱函数，因此我们可以免费恢复系统的近似谱函数，而无需执行解析延拓。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 Hubbard model、dynamical mean field theory 展开。 In this work, we introduce a neural denoiser for fermionic imaginary time Green's functions based on the diffusion model architecture trained on synthetic data.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "在这项工作中，我们基于在合成数据上训练的扩散模型架构，引入了费米子虚数时间格林函数的神经降噪器。我们使用 Bethe 晶格上的半填充 Hubbard 模型、二维 Hubbard 模型的两面片动态聚类近似 (DCA) 以及 SrVO$_3$ 系统对我们的方法进行基准测试。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注Hubbard 模型、动力学平均场理论相关的有效模型参数、电子关联强度、相图边界以及可与实验对照的谱学或输运信号。"
