              "abstractOriginal": "The iron-based ferromagnetic materials have emerged as a promising system for spintronics due to their high Curie temperatures and significant anomalous Hall effect (AHE) driven by Berry curvature. While there have been investigations into the epitaxial growth of non-layered iron-based ferromagnetic materials, the realization of high-quality single crystal thin films continues to be a formidable obstacle. Meanwhile, the issues such as grain boundary scattering further hinder their characterization and application. Here, we report the first chemical vapor deposition (CVD) synthesis of single-crystalline cubic D0$_3$-Fe$_3$Ge nanoplates. This compound represents a substantial departure from the conventional hexagonal phases typically observed in the Fe-Ge system. Structural characterizations confirm the cubic lattice and stoichiometric purity of the crystals. Structural analysis identifies a strong epitaxial effect, resulting in a giant compressive strain of ~4.16% at the interface that relaxes gradually toward the surface. The second-harmonic generation (SHG) signals might further reveal that such interfacial strain disrupted the inherent centro-symmetry of the cubic phase. SQUID magnetometry shows robust room-temperature ferromagnetism and clear magnetic anisotropy. Magneto-transport measurements reveal a robust AHE that remains stable at temperatures far exceeding room temperature. The scaling observed between the anomalous Hall resistance and longitudinal resistance strongly suggests that this effect is dominated by the intrinsic Berry curvature mechanism. Furthermore, density functional theory (DFT) calculations reveal that the huge epitaxial strain induces band reconstructions and creates dense spin-orbit coupling gaps near the Fermi level, effectively doubling the anomalous Hall conductivity to match our experimental observations.",
              "abstractZh": "铁基铁磁材料由于其高居里温度和由贝里曲率驱动的显着反常霍尔效应（AHE）而成为自旋电子学的有前途的系统。尽管人们对非层状铁基铁磁材料的外延生长进行了研究，但高质量单晶薄膜的实现仍然是一个巨大的障碍。同时，晶界散射等问题进一步阻碍了它们的表征和应用。 在这里，我们报告了单晶立方 D0$_3$-Fe$_3$Ge 纳米板的首次化学气相沉积 (CVD) 合成。这种化合物与 Fe-Ge 系统中通常观察到的传统六方相有很大不同。结构表征证实了晶体的立方晶格和化学计量纯度。结构分析发现了强烈的外延效应，导致界面处产生约 4.16% 的巨大压缩应变，并逐渐向表面松弛。 二次谐波产生（SHG）信号可能进一步揭示这种界面应变破坏了立方相固有的中心对称性。 SQUID 磁力测量显示出强大的室温铁磁性和明显的磁各向异性。磁输运测量揭示了强大的 AHE，在远超过室温的温度下仍保持稳定。在反常霍尔电阻和纵向电阻之间观察到的缩放强烈表明这种效应是由固有的贝里曲率机制主导的。 此外，密度泛函理论（DFT）计算表明，巨大的外延应变会引起能带重建，并在费米能级附近产生密集的自旋轨道耦合间隙，有效地使反常霍尔电导率加倍，以匹配我们的实验观察结果。",
              "articleSummary": "The iron-based ferromagnetic materials have emerged as a promising system for spintronics due to their high Curie temperatures and significant anomalous Hall effect (AHE) driven by Berry curvature. While there have been investigations into the epitaxial growth of non-layered iron-based ferromagnetic materials, the realization of high-quality single crystal thin films continues to be a formidable obstacle. Meanwhile, the issues such as grain boundary scattering further hinder their characterization and application. Here, we report the first chemical vapor deposition (CVD) synthesis of single-crystalline cubic D0$_3$-Fe$_3$Ge nanoplates. This compound represents a substantial departure from the conventional hexagonal phases typically observed in the Fe-Ge system. Structural characterizations confirm the cubic lattice and stoichiometric purity of the crystals. Structural analysis identifies a strong epitaxial effect, resulting in a giant compressive strain of ~4.16% at the interface that relaxes gradually toward the surface. The second-harmonic generation (SHG) signals might further reveal that such interfacial strain disrupted the inherent centro-symmetry of the cubic phase. SQUID magnetometry shows robust room-temperature ferromagnetism and clear magnetic anisotropy. Magneto-transport measurements reveal a robust AHE that remains stable at temperatures far exceeding room temperature. The scaling observed between the anomalous Hall resistance and longitudinal resistance strongly suggests that this effect is dominated by the intrinsic Berry curvature mechanism. Furthermore, density functional theory (DFT) calculations reveal that the huge epitaxial strain induces band reconstructions and creates dense spin-orbit coupling gaps near the Fermi level, effectively doubling the anomalous Hall conductivity to match our experimental observations.",
              "articleSummaryZh": "铁基铁磁材料由于其高居里温度和由贝里曲率驱动的显着反常霍尔效应（AHE）而成为自旋电子学的有前途的系统。尽管人们对非层状铁基铁磁材料的外延生长进行了研究，但高质量单晶薄膜的实现仍然是一个巨大的障碍。同时，晶界散射等问题进一步阻碍了它们的表征和应用。 在这里，我们报告了单晶立方 D0$_3$-Fe$_3$Ge 纳米板的首次化学气相沉积 (CVD) 合成。这种化合物与 Fe-Ge 系统中通常观察到的传统六方相有很大不同。结构表征证实了晶体的立方晶格和化学计量纯度。结构分析发现了强烈的外延效应，导致界面处产生约 4.16% 的巨大压缩应变，并逐渐向表面松弛。 二次谐波产生（SHG）信号可能进一步揭示这种界面应变破坏了立方相固有的中心对称性。 SQUID 磁力测量显示出强大的室温铁磁性和明显的磁各向异性。磁输运测量揭示了强大的 AHE，在远超过室温的温度下仍保持稳定。在反常霍尔电阻和纵向电阻之间观察到的缩放强烈表明这种效应是由固有的贝里曲率机制主导的。 此外，密度泛函理论（DFT）计算表明，巨大的外延应变会引起能带重建，并在费米能级附近产生密集的自旋轨道耦合间隙，有效地使反常霍尔电导率加倍，以匹配我们的实验观察结果。",
              "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 ferromagnetism 展开。 While there have been investigations into the epitaxial growth of non-layered iron-based ferromagnetic materials, the realization of high-quality single crystal thin films continues to be a formidable obstacle.",
              "discussionFocusZh": "铁基铁磁材料由于其高居里温度和由贝里曲率驱动的显着反常霍尔效应（AHE）而成为自旋电子学的有前途的系统。尽管人们对非层状铁基铁磁材料的外延生长进行了研究，但高质量单晶薄膜的实现仍然是一个巨大的障碍。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注铁磁性相关的第一性原理设置、对称性分析、能带或响应函数计算，以及这些量与可观测物性的对应关系。"
