          "abstractOriginal": "Electron--electron interactions can reconstruct Bloch wave functions, changing their geometry and the associated thermoelectric response. We derive the linear thermoelectric response within the Hartree--Fock (HF) approximation using the thermal length-gauge density-matrix approach, resolving Drude, symmetric quantum-metric, and antisymmetric Berry-curvature contributions. In a noninteracting Bloch eigenbasis, we separate the reconstructed Berry connection into the noninteracting connection and an interaction connection. This gives bare, coherence, and interaction-connection contributions to the anomalous thermoelectric response. We determine the constraints imposed by spatial inversion, rotational, time-reversal, and combined symmetries on the three transport channels. In the relaxation-time approximation, the leading weak-broadening behavior is $Γ^{-1}$ for the Drude contribution, $Γ$ for the quantum-metric contribution, and $Γ^0$ for the Berry-curvature contribution. The interband scalings apply away from band degeneracies. Self-consistent calculations for the triangular-lattice extended Hubbard model illustrate how interactions generate Berry curvature and a quantum metric, change the symmetry of the system, and thereby contribute to transverse thermoelectric transport.",
          "abstractZh": "电子-电子相互作用可以重建布洛赫波函数，改变它们的几何形状和相关的热电响应。我们使用热长度规范密度矩阵方法推导出 Hartree--Fock (HF) 近似内的线性热电响应，解决了 Drude、对称量子度量和反对称 Berry 曲率贡献。在非交互的 Bloch 特征基中，我们将重建的 Berry 连接分为非交互连接和交互连接。 这为异常热电响应提供了裸露、相干和相互作用连接的贡献。我们确定空间反转、旋转、时间反转和组合对称性对三个传输通道施加的约束。在弛豫时间近似中，主要的弱展宽行为是 Drude 贡献的 $Г^{-1}$、量子度量贡献的 $Г$ 和 Berry 曲率贡献的 $Г^0$。带间缩放适用于远离带简并性的情况。 三角晶格扩展哈伯德模型的自洽计算说明了相互作用如何产生贝里曲率和量子度量，改变系统的对称性，从而有助于横向热电传输。",
          "articleSummary": "Electron--electron interactions can reconstruct Bloch wave functions, changing their geometry and the associated thermoelectric response. We derive the linear thermoelectric response within the Hartree--Fock (HF) approximation using the thermal length-gauge density-matrix approach, resolving Drude, symmetric quantum-metric, and antisymmetric Berry-curvature contributions. In a noninteracting Bloch eigenbasis, we separate the reconstructed Berry connection into the noninteracting connection and an interaction connection. This gives bare, coherence, and interaction-connection contributions to the anomalous thermoelectric response. We determine the constraints imposed by spatial inversion, rotational, time-reversal, and combined symmetries on the three transport channels. In the relaxation-time approximation, the leading weak-broadening behavior is $Γ^{-1}$ for the Drude contribution, $Γ$ for the quantum-metric contribution, and $Γ^0$ for the Berry-curvature contribution. The interband scalings apply away from band degeneracies. Self-consistent calculations for the triangular-lattice extended Hubbard model illustrate how interactions generate Berry curvature and a quantum metric, change the symmetry of the system, and thereby contribute to transverse thermoelectric transport.",
          "articleSummaryZh": "电子-电子相互作用可以重建布洛赫波函数，改变它们的几何形状和相关的热电响应。我们使用热长度规范密度矩阵方法推导出 Hartree--Fock (HF) 近似内的线性热电响应，解决了 Drude、对称量子度量和反对称 Berry 曲率贡献。在非交互的 Bloch 特征基中，我们将重建的 Berry 连接分为非交互连接和交互连接。 这为异常热电响应提供了裸露、相干和相互作用连接的贡献。我们确定空间反转、旋转、时间反转和组合对称性对三个传输通道施加的约束。在弛豫时间近似中，主要的弱展宽行为是 Drude 贡献的 $Г^{-1}$、量子度量贡献的 $Г$ 和 Berry 曲率贡献的 $Г^0$。带间缩放适用于远离带简并性的情况。 三角晶格扩展哈伯德模型的自洽计算说明了相互作用如何产生贝里曲率和量子度量，改变系统的对称性，从而有助于横向热电传输。",
          "discussionFocus": "重点围绕 Hubbard model 展开。 We derive the linear thermoelectric response within the Hartree--Fock (HF) approximation using the thermal length-gauge density-matrix approach, resolving Drude, symmetric quantum-metric, and antisymmetric Berry-curvature contributions.",
          "discussionFocusZh": "我们使用热长度规范密度矩阵方法推导出 Hartree--Fock (HF) 近似内的线性热电响应，解决了 Drude、对称量子度量和反对称 Berry 曲率贡献。在非交互的 Bloch 特征基中，我们将重建的 Berry 连接分为非交互连接和交互连接。 结合关键词看，阅读时应重点关注Hubbard 模型相关的有效模型参数、电子关联强度、相图边界以及可与实验对照的谱学或输运信号。"
