          "abstractOriginal": "Magnetism in transition-metal dichalcogenide monolayers has attracted considerable attention, yet its nature remains elusive, particularly in monolayer 1T-VSe$_2$. Our first-principles calculations show that Stoner instability can drive ferromagnetism in XS$_2$ and XSe$_2$ monolayers (X = Ti, V, Co, Mo, and Ru), associated with a reduced density of states at the Fermi level. We demonstrate that mixing nonmagnetic Ti, Co, Mo, and Ru disulfides or diselenides can induce magnetism. Conversely, mixing magnetic VS$_2$ or VSe$_2$ with other compounds can completely suppress magnetism. Both scenarios can lower the total energy. Moreover, substituting a small number of V atoms with Co defects can also disrupt ferromagnetism in 1T-V(S,Se)$_2$. Even in pristine 1T-VSe$_2$, we find ferrimagnetic configurations with reversed local V moments that are nearly degenerate with the ferromagnetic state. Their competition may contribute to the suppression of long-range ferromagnetic order. This reduced energy penalty for magnetic and structural disorder arises from a suppressed density of states at the Fermi level, resembling the mechanism underlying the Peierls transition. Electronically driven energy lowering near the Fermi level may therefore be widespread among transition-metal dichalcogenide monolayers in various forms.",
          "abstractZh": "过渡金属二硫属化物单层中的磁性引起了相当大的关注，但其性质仍然难以捉摸，特别是在单层 1T-VSe$_2$ 中。我们的第一原理计算表明，斯托纳不稳定性可以驱动 XS$_2$ 和 XSe$_2$ 单层（X = Ti、V、Co、Mo 和 Ru）中的铁磁性，与费米能级态密度的降低相关。我们证明，混合非磁性钛、钴、钼和钌二硫化物或二硒化物可以产生磁性。相反，将磁性VS$_2$或VSe$_2$与其他化合物混合可以完全抑制磁性。 两种情况都可以降低总能量。此外，用Co缺陷取代少量V原子也可以破坏1T-V(S,Se)$_2$中的铁磁性。即使在原始的 1T-VSe$_2$ 中，我们也发现了具有反向局部 V 矩的亚铁磁结构，这些结构几乎随着铁磁态而退化。它们的竞争可能有助于抑制长程铁磁有序。磁性和结构无序的能量损失减少是由于费米能级的态密度受到抑制，类似于佩尔斯转变的机制。 因此，电子驱动的能量降低到费米能级附近可能在各种形式的过渡金属二硫属化物单层中广泛存在。",
