            "abstractOriginal": "Abstract Enzymes catalyze complex chemical transformations with remarkable efficiency and selectivity, yet their atomistic mechanisms remain challenging to capture because conventional simulations trade accuracy for efficiency. Here we introduce a reactive machine learning/molecular mechanics (ML/MM) framework that bridges quantum chemistry with long-timescale sampling, enabling direct exploration of enzymatic transition states and free-energy landscapes. Coupled with metadynamics, this approach achieves nanosecond sampling of bond-forming reactions and quantitatively predicts activation barriers, mutational effects, and stereoselectivity. Applied to Diels-Alderases, the framework not only reproduces experimental activity and endo / exo preferences with sub-kcal mol −1 accuracy but also uncovers how pathway dynamics and local electrostatics preorganize substrates for selective outcomes. By uniting reactivity, conformational dynamics, and predictive power, this work establishes reactive ML/MM as a broadly applicable strategy for mechanistic enzymology and a foundation for the rational design of new biocatalysts.",
            "abstractZh": "摘要 酶以显着的效率和选择性催化复杂的化学转化，但其原子机制仍然难以捕捉，因为传统的模拟以准确性换取效率。在这里，我们介绍了一种反应式机器学习/分子力学 (ML/MM) 框架，该框架将量子化学与长时间尺度采样联系起来，从而能够直接探索酶过渡态和自由能景观。 与元动力学相结合，该方法实现了成键反应的纳秒采样，并定量预测激活障碍、突变效应和立体选择性。应用于 Diels-Alderases 时，该框架不仅以亚 kcal mol -1 的精度再现实验活性和内切/外切偏好，而且还揭示了通路动力学和局部静电如何预组织底物以获得选择性结果。 通过结合反应性、构象动力学和预测能力，这项工作将反应性 ML/MM 确立为机械酶学的广泛适用策略，并为新型生物催化剂的合理设计奠定了基础。",
